<h2>The baseline: title decides</h2>
<p>When a marriage ends, each spouse leaves with what the law already recognises as theirs: assets in their name, purchases from their funds, inheritances and gifts received individually. Divorce decrees under the Hindu Marriage Act dissolve the marital status; they do not pool or partition wealth. Every equitable adjustment happens through a specific statutory door &mdash; and each door has its own forum, proof and limits.</p>

<h2>The five instruments</h2>
<table class="law">
  <tr><th>Instrument</th><th>Reaches</th><th>Forum</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Section 27 HMA</td><td>Property presented at or about the marriage, jointly belonging to both</td><td>The matrimonial court, in the main petition</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Stridhan</td><td>Everything given to or earned by the wife as her own — absolute ownership</td><td>DV Act proceedings, criminal process, or civil suit</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Permanent alimony (Section 25 HMA)</td><td>A maintenance sum or periodic payment, securable as a charge on the respondent&rsquo;s property</td><td>The matrimonial court, at or after decree</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Residence orders (DV Act, Section 19)</td><td>The right to reside in or be rehoused from the shared household — occupation, not ownership</td><td>Magistrate under the DV Act</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Civil ownership claims</td><td>Funded purchases in the other spouse&rsquo;s name, joint acquisitions, partition of genuinely co-owned assets</td><td>Civil court, on the money trail</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Using Section 27 well</h2>
<div class="flow">
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Inventory early.</strong> The provision works on identifiable articles — list the wedding gifts, appliances, vehicles and valuables with dates, givers and locations while memories and photographs are fresh.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Plead it in the petition.</strong> Section 27 relief rides with the matrimonial case; raising it late, or after decree, surrenders the convenience the section exists to provide.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Distinguish the categories.</strong> Items that are the wife&rsquo;s stridhan are hers absolutely and need no joint-belonging analysis; Section 27 does the work for the genuinely joint residue.</div>
</div>

<h2>Settlement practice in Delhi</h2>
<p>Because the default rules are blunt, most property questions in matrimonial disputes are resolved by negotiated settlement &mdash; recorded in mutual consent petitions under Section 13B or in mediation settlements that courts incorporate. A well-drafted settlement specifies each asset and its destination, records the stridhan as returned against an itemised receipt, deals with joint accounts, lockers and vehicle transfers, and contains the cross-undertakings on pending and future claims. The cases that return to court years later are almost always the ones whose settlements spoke in round figures and generalities.</p>
<div class="note">This explainer describes the general legal framework for information. It is not legal advice; property outcomes depend on title, funding and documentation in each marriage.</div>
